WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.540
Whether it's working on a classic Stephen
King movie or one of his more frowned-upon

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.720
films, getting involved with the King of Horror
can make a star, revive a career, or give

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.000
an actor a new perspective.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.720
From helpful psychics to horrified housewives,
these King roles changed these actors forever.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.600
Carrie was the first screen adaptation of
a Stephen King story, and it remains one of

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.460
the most iconic.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:25.240
The film launched several careers, but the
person who owes the most to the movie is Sissy

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:25.740
Spacek.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.140
The movie almost single-handedly turned her
into a celebrity.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.440
Spacek first drew attention in Terrence Malick's
Badlands, but still wasn't quite a star yet

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.680
when the movie was released in 1973.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.140
Hearing that Stephen King's Carrie was getting
adapted for a movie, Spacek used her familiarity

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.000
with the book to her advantage and auditioned
for the title role.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.120
The director had another actress in mind,
but Spacek's audition was so good that it

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:49.830
blew everyone else out of the water.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.860
The role earned Spacek popular acclaim and
an Oscar nomination… but maybe it's a good

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.440
thing that she didn't actually win.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.140
The last time she was onstage receiving an
honor, things got a little freaky.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.540
Anthony Michael Hall was one of the biggest
young stars of the 1980s.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.660
A regular actor for teen movie director John
Hughes, a veteran of the Vacation franchise,

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:20.009
and a brief cast member of Saturday Night
Live, his career seemed bulletproof.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:23.200
Then came the '90s and Hall's career seriously
tapered off.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.300
He spent most of the decade doing guest TV
appearances and showing up in less-successful

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:27.800
movies.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.440
Hall was at a professional low point in 2001.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.109
He co-starred in Freddy Got Fingered and critics
had some pretty harsh things to say about

00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:35.600
the film.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.100
"It sucks!"

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:42.240
A year later, he managed to snag the lead
role in a TV show based on Stephen King's

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.240
book, The Dead Zone.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.340
For six seasons, Hall played the part of Johnny
Smith, a man who wakes up from a coma with

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.120
psychic powers.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.420
During its run, The Dead Zone was one of the
highest-rated shows on basic cable.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.859
After years of misses, Hall had a hit again,
and he's credited The Dead Zone with turning

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:58.840
his career around.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.439
If Shelley Duvall's performance as a woman
driven to the edge of sanity in The Shining

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.000
seems like an authentic depiction of terror,
it's because it is.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.219
Director Stanley Kubrick was a noted perfectionist
and his demanding style made her very emotional

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:12.720
on set.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.000
One shot famously took 127 takes, allegedly
in part because Kubrick wanted to push Duvall

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.280
to the point of breaking down.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.860
Even though shooting the film was, by all
accounts, a horrible experience, Duvall's

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.170
performance was so memorable, she soon became
a very well-known actor.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.120
She told People magazine in 1981...

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.120
"When somebody recognizes you at a Dairy Queen
in Texas, you're a star."

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:39.349
After the torturous atmosphere of The Shining,
Duvall was more than happy to star opposite

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:44.120
the kind-hearted Robin Williams in her next
role, that of Olive Oyl in Robert Altman's

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:44.620
Popeye.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.820
Not many films can boast a cast like Stand
by Me.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:52.640
Fewer films can claim to be the starting point
for no less than four successful acting careers.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.920
Based on Stephen King's novella The Body,
Stand by Me tells the story of four boys searching

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.209
for a corpse in the woods.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:04.220
And the four kids in question were played
by new teenage actors Wil Wheaton, Jerry O'Connell,

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.620
Corey Feldman, and River Phoenix.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.680
As for Wil Wheaton, Stand By Me was his first
major movie role, and he'd join the cast of

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.740
Star Trek: The Next Generation soon after.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.630
He's since gone on to become something of
a geek icon, epitomized by playing a version

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.280
of himself on The Big Bang Theory.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.719
It was also the first movie role of Jerry
O'Connell, who would go on to a solid acting

00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:26.889
career on stage and screen, with perhaps his
most prominent role being in the cast of the

00:03:26.889 --> 00:03:28.220
sci-fi show Sliders.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.579
Corey Feldman was the most established star
in Stand by Me, having already appeared in

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.560
Gremlins and The Goonies, but he continued
to be extremely successful for the rest of

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.180
the decade.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.140
Although his career peaked in the '80s, Feldman
had already amassed an impressive body of

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:44.260
work and definitely made the most of his time
in the spotlight.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.100
"I'm in the prime of my youth, and I'll only
be young once!"

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.580
"Yeah, but you're gonna be stupid for the
rest of your life."

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.720
And, of course, there's River Phoenix, whose
work in the film helped sell it to wary distributors.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.040
Coming out of this movie, he was pegged as
the "next big thing."

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.900
He acted in several high-profile movies, including
Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade and My

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:09.500
Own Private Idaho, before his tragic death
by overdose at the young age of 23.

00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:13.820
Although more experienced than many of his
fellow cast members, Stand by Me also featured

00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:17.510
a breakout performance from another fresh
face, Kiefer Sutherland, who would become

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.960
a major star just a year later with his role
in The Lost Boys.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:26.140
Morgan Freeman, the actor, is a huge star,
but Morgan Freeman, the voice, is arguably

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.400
even more well-known.

00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:31.620
As a performer, his calm but authoritative
demeanor has seen him play everyone from a

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.580
humble chauffeur in Driving Miss Daisy to
God himself in Bruce Almighty.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.139
As a narrator, he's voiced over everything
from Oscar-winning documentaries like March

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.760
of the Penguins to the Discovery Channel's
Curiosity.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.400
And his career as a voiceover artist can be
traced back to a Stephen King role the inmate

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.910
Red in The Shawshank Redemption.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:54.000
Based on a novella from the King collection
Different Seasons, the 1994 film had Freeman

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.040
pulling double duty.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:59.300
Not only was he one of the main characters,
he was also narrated the entire movie and

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.600
delivered some of its most iconic lines.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.900
I hope the Pacific is as blue as it is in
my dreams…

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:08.960
I hope."

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.800
While The Shawshank Redemption bombed financially
in theaters, it picked up a second life on

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.560
TV and in the rental market, eventually becoming
a massively beloved film for fans around the

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.060
world.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.240
Many years later, Freeman was a guest on Graham
Norton's talk show and he poked a little fun

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.540
at his reputation as a master of narration.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.420
"I hope people stop asking me to do stupid
voiceovers.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:34.840
I hope."

